  "modelingNotes": [
    "Los Angeles Central Library (1926, Bertram Goodhue; Tom Bradley wing 1993, Hardy Holzman Pfeiffer), Los Angeles — original procedural geometry, CC0-1.0. bun generators/la-central-library.ts [out.glb]",
    "Map frame: x east, y north, z up, metres; origin at the outline's centroid on the lowest ground under it (the Grand Ave side). Placed at bearing 38.5°, so the block is square to this frame: +x faces Grand Avenue, −x Flower Street, +y 5th Street.",
    "What makes it the library: Goodhue's cream concrete block, stepping up in setbacks to a central square tower whose shaft is cut by tall window bays, crowned by a tiled pyramid (gold sun mosaic) carrying a hand holding a torch. East of it, sharing its outline, the Tom Bradley wing: a plain cream block of the same height with a glazed atrium in its roof.",
    "Sources:",
    "Plan: OSM way/428021732 (both buildings in one outline), its parts way/495571355 (the central block under the tower) and way/1106887040 (the Bradley wing).",
    "Heights: LA County LARIAC 2006 lidar surface model (Elevation MapServer layer 8, 3 m grid) over the bare-earth low point 85.4 m at the Grand Ave side: Goodhue's main block 24 m (≈ 18 m over 5th St and Flower St, which stand ≈ 6 m higher), the central block 30–33 m, the shaft's top ≈ 46 m, the pyramid ≈ 51 m on a 3 m grid; LARIAC 2020 footprint 484322840870 gives the top (torch) at 142.2 m, 56.8 m over y = 0. Bradley wing's roof 24–26 m, its north terraces 14–20 m.",
    "Proportions of the tower, pyramid and finial, the window bays, colours: photos (Wikimedia Commons) — \"Los-angeles-central-library\" (Mfield, GFDL 1.2, the 5th St front, square on); HABS CAL,19-LOSAN,65-7 \"General view, west elevation\" and 65-2 \"Looking SW from across West Fifth St.\", 65-4 \"Distant view, east side\" (Marvin Rand, public domain); \"Los Angeles Central Library 08\" (Visitor7, CC BY-SA 3.0).",
    "Estimated: the shaft's width (15 m, lidar and photo), the stage's steps, the pyramid's pitch (7 m high on a 14.6 m base) and its two-tone sun pattern, from the photos scaled by the lidar heights; the window bays' heights; the torch is drawn as a gilded post and flame.",
    "Left out: the sculpture, inscriptions, the Maguire Gardens and the stairs.",
    "Original procedural model from https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks (catalog id \"la-central-library\", model \"la-central-library\"), generated by https://github.com/alexwohlbruck/landmarks/blob/c3921f733df14b41e1f6d15853cce7b343886f17/generators/la-central-library.ts. That repository is the editable source; source.blend.gz is the exported mesh imported into Blender for convenience.",
    "Exported for Open Landmarks v1: placement bearing and scale baked in; moving parts frozen in their rest pose; footings and basements below the lowest ground (y = 0) cut away; material colours carried over exactly, as library finishes where they are not standard swatches."
  ],
